# Intermediates from tools/prepare.sh live in /tmp, not here.

# IMPORTANT — if this repo is ever public, do NOT commit stems separated from
# the real M83 recording. Academic use of the track in a demo is one thing;
# publishing the separated audio is distributing the recording. Either keep the
# repo private, or uncomment the next line before adding the real stems.
# content/panel-01/stems/

# Encoded web stems (~59 MB) ARE tracked — the repo is private and the use is
# academic, and the demo is useless without them.

# The raw multitrack exports are not: 1.1 GB, with single files at 45 MB.
# Git would be unusable and they are only needed to re-run encode_stems.sh.
# Keep them backed up somewhere outside the repo.
# Leading slash matters: macOS matches paths case-insensitively, so an
# unanchored "STEMS/" also swallows content/*/stems/.
/STEMS/
